<!-- Composed from Material Symbols Outlined "sort" + "arrow_downward", both at wght 700 (Apache-2.0).
     Material Symbols ships no directional sort glyph (google/material-design-icons#189), so the two
     stock paths are laid out side by side with group transforms rather than redrawn by hand. Both
     groups take the SAME uniform scale, which is what keeps the bars and the arrow's shaft at one
     stroke weight; the wght 700 source (125/126 units thick, vs the default weight's 80) is what
     leaves that weight at ~1.7px once scaled, close to the 2px of the default-weight icons this
     one sits beside in the toolbar. Scaling only one group, or scaling either non-uniformly, breaks
     one of those two properties. Resulting layout: bars x 47..481, arrow x 523..913 (symmetric
     47-unit side insets, 43-unit gap), both centred on y 480. -->
